{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This trip's own GPS trace establishes the deviation, and by a wide margin. gps_trace.trace_distance_km on EV-GPS-00507 is 11.36 km against a booked optimal of 3.6 km carried on EV-TRIP-00507, an excess of 7.76 km — 215.6% of the optimal route (derived.deviation.excess_km and derived.deviation.excess_pct on EV-GPS-00507). Both POL-RD-01 establishment gates are cleared: the excess is far greater than 20% of optimal_distance_km and far greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms. Because the excess also exceeds 50% of the optimal distance, this is additionally a MATERIAL deviation. POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure the governing measurement and expressly bars trip_record.actual_distance_km, a rounded convenience copy, from the threshold test — so the finding is safe on the trace figure, and would be safe on the rounded figure too.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00507", "EV-TRIP-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes, so the deviation can stand on it alone. EV-GPS-00507 is admissibility-COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, carries 127 fixes at a 10 second cadence with 100% coverage, reports no gaps at all and a max_gap_sec of 0.0. None of POL-RD-07's impairment limbs (a) to (c) fires. The independent-corroboration requirement in POL-RD-07(ii), and the escalation that would follow from it under POL-RD-10(3), are therefore not engaged, and no discount attaches to the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged on the face of the bundle. The trip_record, the gps_trace and the fare_breakdown all carry the same trip identifier TRP-00507 and describe the same pickup event, and the excess is measured from a trace that is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c). The additional-corroboration proviso in POL-RD-08 does not bite either: EV-RPROF-00507 shows rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d of 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated of 0, far below the 4-and-1 threshold. No profile field beyond those the clause names is relied on; under POL-GEN-01 the profiles go only to how closely assertions are scrutinised, never to a fact about this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00507", "EV-GPS-00507", "EV-FARE-00507", "EV-RPROF-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic-advisory exoneration is available, and the absence is itself the evidence. EV-ADVIS-00507-01 is MISSING: its payload is null, its weight_multiplier is 0.0, and the pre-pass records a blocking MISSING_ARTIFACT issue — 'No advisory covers Airport Boulevard or Changi Coast Rd in this window.' A missing artifact can carry no fact, but under POL-GEN-02(3) its absence is citable, and the driver's side points to no advisory ID at all. POL-RD-03 exonerates only where an advisory names a road the optimal route traverses within a validity window, and there is no advisory to run that test on. Nothing about this detour is exonerated.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00507-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No rider-requested-detour exoneration is available. The chat log for this trip, EV-CHAT-00507, is admissibility-COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and contains zero messages — message_count 0 with an empty messages array. POL-RD-04 requires an instruction from the rider recorded in the chat_log, timestamped before the vehicle leaves the optimal corridor or at most three minutes after, identifying a place or road specifically enough to act on. No such message exists, and because there is no chat message there is no chat_message.waypoint_hint against which the 200 m corroboration test could be run, so that test is undecidable and the clause is unavailable on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No relocation exoneration is available either. EV-TRIP-00507 shows pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at both null, and amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min both null, so the POL-RD-05 re-quote does not exist and the clause cannot be run on this record. Nor is this a pooled trip: vehicle_type is RYDE_TAXI, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline has no application and the booked optimal of 3.6 km is the correct baseline for the threshold test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's explanation names no artifact and carries no weight. His account that Changi Beach is very long, that the rider could not say which car park, and that he 'chose a quiet spot', is an assertion that identifies no evidence ID on either the route or the destination. POL-RD-08 is explicit that assertions from either side which cite no evidence ID are discarded; the empty chat log at EV-CHAT-00507 confirms no rider instruction exists to support it, and 'the meter is the meter' is not a defence, because POL-RD-02 fixes the refund arithmetically against the optimal route rather than against what was metered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00507", "EV-FARE-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic and the figures are these, stated on separate lines as POL-RD-02 requires. charged_total is 25.03 (EV-FARE-00507; payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 3.6 optimal km + 0.28 x 7.0 optimal min) x the surge_multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = (3.80 + 2.70 + 1.96) = 8.46, plus 0.80 platform fee = 9.26, plus the fixed Changi Airport surcharge of 6.00 already itemised and properly chargeable on a trip originating at the airport = 15.26; no ERP or toll charge arises, waiting_time_fee is 0.00 and promo_discount is 0.00. The refund is 25.03 − 15.26 = 9.77, rounded UP to SGD 9.80. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and 39.0% of charged_total, below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 9.80.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00507", "EV-TRIP-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No separate pass-through correction arises, and the rider claims none on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. The 6.00 airport surcharge is properly chargeable because this trip ORIGINATES at Changi Airport Terminal 3, so POL-RD-09(4)'s billing-integrity correction does not bite on that line. Every ERP total on the fare_breakdown is 0.00 and the erp_gantries list is empty, so there is nothing for POL-RD-09 to add. POL-RD-09(1) forbids stacking off-route ERP on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, and the rider does not ask for it: the single refund of SGD 9.80 is the whole of the money sought.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00507", "EV-TRIP-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the deviation is MATERIAL, POL-RD-06 requires the driver_profile check, and it must be run on the field the clause names. EV-DPROF-00507 shows driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d of 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 250 — the trailing-90-day counter, not the lifetime prior_deviation_flags (also 0), which POL-RD-06 and POL-GEN-01 forbid substituting. Neither the 3-flag gate nor the 0.05-ratio gate is met, so no repeat pattern is established and no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) follow. The rider does not claim either, and the POL-RD-02 partial of SGD 9.80 stands as the remedy on this trip's own evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00507", "EV-GPS-00507"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 9.8,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The route-deviation finding rests on this trip's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00507, weight 1.0): 11.36 km driven against the booked optimal of 3.6 km on EV-TRIP-00507, an excess of 7.76 km, or 215.6% of the optimal route. POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure the governing measurement (the trip record's rounded 11.4 km may not be cited), and both establishment gates (>20% and >0.8 km) plus the materiality gate (>50%) are cleared, so the deviation is established and MATERIAL. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07: 127 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0 — so no independent corroboration is needed and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged.\n\nNo exoneration applies. There is no traffic advisory to run POL-RD-03 on: EV-ADVIS-00507-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, blocking MISSING_ARTIFACT), can carry no fact, and its absence exonerates nothing. The chat log EV-CHAT-00507 is complete and empty (0 messages), so there is no rider instruction and no chat_message.waypoint_hint against which POL-RD-04's 200 m corroboration test could run — the clause is unavailable on this record, as it says. No pickup or dropoff amendment exists, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run, and the vehicle is RYDE_TAXI, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline has no application.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, and both sides compute it identically. Charged total 25.03 (EV-FARE-00507; payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued 0.00). Recomputed fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 × 3.6 km + 0.28 × 7.0 min) × the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = (3.80 + 2.70 + 1.96) = 8.46, plus the 0.80 platform fee, plus the SGD 6.00 Changi Airport surcharge. That surcharge is properly chargeable because the trip ORIGINATES at Changi Airport Terminal 3 and ran off-peak (Wednesday midday), so POL-RD-09(4) does not bite. No ERP or toll lines arise (all totals 0.00, erp_gantries empty), waiting_time_fee is 0.00 and promo_discount is 0.00, giving a recomputed fare of 15.26. Refund = 25.03 − 15.26 = 9.77, rounded UP to SGD 9.80. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and 39.0% of the charge, short of the 90% that would make it a FULL_REFUND, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 9.80. Nothing is added on top: POL-RD-09(1) forbids stacking off-route charges onto a POL-RD-02 refund that already comprehends them, and there is nothing in any event.\n\nThe material deviation made the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check compulsory, and it comes back clean: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250, so neither the 3-flag test nor the 0.05-ratio test is met. There is therefore no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. POL-GEN-01 confines this test to those two fields; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter that both sides mentioned is context only and was correctly not substituted for it, and no other profile field carried any finding.\n\nTwo things the rider raised move no money. The complaint about where the dropoff actually was — 'the beach is over there' — has no evidentiary anchor: the recorded dropoff is Nicoll Drive, Changi, neither endpoint carries an amendment timestamp, and no artifact identifies the point the rider wanted. A finding on that would rest on general geography, which is not evidence, and no clause in this category gives a remedy for it beyond the distance arithmetic already applied. The rider's account of the conversation is likewise uncorroborated: the chat log is empty. The driver's account ('she couldn't tell me which car park ... I chose a quiet spot ... the meter is the meter') cites no artifact and carries no weight, and the metered amount is not the measure — POL-RD-02 fixes the refund against the optimal route, not against what was metered.\n\nConfidence is 0.95: every artifact carrying a deciding fact — the trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown — sits at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers match (TRP-00507 throughout), the trace is unimpaired, no timestamps disagree, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact, and the refund is below both the SGD 150.00 ceiling and the charged total. No clause produces a referral in this case."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
